Z||000000||VISCERAL||09-12-2001||10:08 PM||||Did you have to take it to the shop to get them removed and pressed back in. Anyone done it on their own or is it a shop procedure only.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jay||09-12-2001||10:12 PM||||I did it on my own.  Definately easier if you have the pressing tool.  A new one can't be put in properly unless you have the tool.  <P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||VISCERAL||09-12-2001||10:15 PM||||How much did you pay for your ball joint tool and from where?||||reg||1
Z||000003||2birds||09-12-2001||10:36 PM||||Some guys have reported (here on the Forum) that theirs are tack welded, too.  Mine weren't, so I just used a hydraulic press and a couple short pieces of scrap exhaust pipe I found in a scrap bin at the shop.  A real PITA, worth paying a shop to do if I had to again.  <BR>Try Autozone for a loaner tool; I heard they and others loan tools if you buy the parts from them.||||reg||1
